  "sentences": [
    {
      "start": 0.45,
      "end": 5.091,
      "text": "In 2025, Starbucks reported over two hundred and twenty-two million dollars in revenue."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.321,
      "end": 8.535,
      "text": "From gift-card money customers were never expected to spend."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.765,
      "end": 10.55,
      "text": "And here's the surprising part."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.45,
      "end": 17.999,
      "text": "This isn't some illegal trick. It's a recognized accounting practice used by businesses that sell gift cards."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.229,
      "end": 24.779,
      "text": "Once you see how it works, you'll never look at a gift card the same way again."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.009,
      "end": 26.55,
      "text": "So here's the setup."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.45,
      "end": 32.959,
      "text": "A man walks into Starbucks and buys a twenty-dollar gift card for his friend."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.189,
      "end": 35.55,
      "text": "Starbucks takes his twenty dollars immediately."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.45,
      "end": 39.873,
      "text": "But in accounting terms, that money isn't revenue yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.103,
      "end": 41.244,
      "text": "It's a promise."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.474,
      "end": 45.277,
      "text": "Because Starbucks still owes someone twenty dollars' worth of coffee."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.507,
      "end": 48.55,
      "text": "It's a debt wearing a gift card's clothing."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.45,
      "end": 52.972,
      "text": "Now, the friend visits Starbucks and spends fourteen dollars."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.202,
      "end": 55.55,
      "text": "Six dollars remain on the card."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.45,
      "end": 57.318,
      "text": "Weeks pass."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.548,
      "end": 58.415,
      "text": "Then months."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.645,
      "end": 62.55,
      "text": "And the card ends up forgotten in a drawer."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.45,
      "end": 66.058,
      "text": "Now multiply that by millions of customers."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.288,
      "end": 67.778,
      "text": "Some spend every cent."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.008,
      "end": 70.615,
      "text": "Others leave a dollar or two behind."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.845,
      "end": 77.55,
      "text": "Starbucks studies historical redemption patterns to estimate how much of that money customers are unlikely to ever use."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.45,
      "end": 81.07,
      "text": "And here's where things get interesting."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.3,
      "end": 90.47,
      "text": "Under accounting rules, Starbucks can gradually recognize a portion of those expected unused balances as revenue, in proportion to gift-card redemptions."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.7,
      "end": 92.447,
      "text": "This has a name."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.677,
      "end": 93.55,
      "text": "Gift-card breakage."
    },
    {
      "start": 94.45,
      "end": 100.767,
      "text": "And in fiscal 2025, Starbucks recognized over two hundred and twenty-two million dollars in breakage revenue."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.997,
      "end": 104.55,
      "text": "Not one extra latte required for those unused balances."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.45,
      "end": 107.309,
      "text": "So here's the strange truth."
    },
    {
      "start": 107.539,
      "end": 114.231,
      "text": "A company can recognize revenue even when the customer never comes back to use the remaining gift-card balance."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.461,
      "end": 118.55,
      "text": "The cash was collected earlier. The product may never be redeemed."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.45,
      "end": 123.745,
      "text": "So next time you buy a gift card, ask yourself..."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.975,
      "end": 126.123,
      "text": "Who's really receiving the gift?"
    },
    {
      "start": 126.353,
      "end": 128.93,
      "text": "The person you're giving it to?"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.16,
      "end": 132.166,
      "text": "Or the company you bought it from?"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.396,
      "end": 137.55,
      "text": "Follow Oddly Logical for more strange business secrets hiding in plain sight."
    }
  ],
